Article 1.2 Objectives
ChessBlitz YorkU’s objectives are:
* providing chess-related events;
* providing chess-related education; 
* assisting and encouraging chess-related discussion; 
* encouraging members to participate in events and contributing to the growing popularity of the game of chess; and
* increasing awareness of the game of chess to York University students, staff and faculty.

1. The Executive Committee:
   a. is the only ChessBlitz YorkU committee;
   b. is composed of all executives with the exception of Community Managers and the Chief Returning Officer.

1. Executive Meetings:
   a. are held no less than once a month during the Fall, Winter and Summer terms
   b. are called and chaired by the ChessBlitz YorkU Presidents;
   c. have at least a 4-day prior notice;
   d. have its agenda set by the ChessBlitz YorkU Presidents;
   e. have voting privileges for all members of the executives committee;
   f. have speaking privileges for all executives
   g. have the ChessBlitz YorkU Presidents decide the outcome of a tie vote;
   h. request that every executive attend. If an executive is unable to attend, they must inform the ChessBlitz YorkU Presidents at least 2 days before the meeting; and
   i. are conducted according to the decision of the ChessBlitz YorkU Presidents.
2. General Meetings:
   a. are held once per Fall and Winter term to show ChessBlitz YorkU financial statements and discuss the work of ChessBlitz YorkU;
   b. are open to all ChessBlitz YorkU members, non-members and executives;
   c. are called and chaired by the ChessBlitz YorkU Presidents;
   d. have at least a 7-day prior notice;
   e. have its agenda set by the ChessBlitz YorkU Presidents;
   f. have voting and speaking privileges for all ChessBlitz YorkU members; and
   g. are conducted according to the decision of the ChessBlitz YorkU Presidents.

Article 8.3 President
* The position is limited to two (2) individuals who previously served a full term as an executive member
The President must:
* Direct how Article 1.2 will be met;
* Ensure Article 1.2 is met;
* Approve or deny plans for ChessBlitz YorkU events;
* Decide whether ChessBlitz YorkU should participate in an external event;
* Manage the ChessBlitz YorkU email;
* Act as the main representative of the club;
* Be familiar with the financial procedures;
* Work with the Financial Coordinator to ensure sustainability of the club;
* Apply for funding from other organizations (YFS, SCLD)
* Ensure that all executive members of the club are acting accordingly and fulfilling their responsibilities and duties; and
* Handle conflict of interest and allegations of wrongdoing cases.

Article 8.4 Financial Coordinator
* This position limited to one (1) individual who previously served a full term as an executive member
The Financial Coordinator must:
* Keep accurate and complete records of the finances of the club;
* Prepare a budget, an opening financial report, and a closing financial report for the club for each term and present them to the executive members;
* Prepare a Financial Statement to be used for YFS re-ratification;
* Present up-to-date financial reports at each executive meeting;
* Maintain an accounting ledger and record all club transactions/reimbursements;
* Check the accuracy and consistency of the previous term's financial records at the beginning of each term; and
* Host Finance meetings before any event that requires financial aid and discuss spending the club budget on events if necessary.

Article 8.5 Event Manager
* This position is limited to four (4) individuals
The Event Manager must:
* Plan, organize, manage, and host ChessBlitz YorkU events;
* Work with other ChessBlitz YorkU Executives to achieve successful planning and organization of events;
* Seek approval from the ChessBlitz YorkU Presidents for the plan of a ChessBlitz YorkU event;
* Organize and allocate resources such as booking rooms, snacks, drinks, and other supplies; and
* Be an effective communicator.

Article 8.6 Social Media Coordinator
* This position is limited to three (3) individuals
The Social Media Coordinator must:
* Plan, design and create social media communications to club members through relevant social media outlets;
* Coordinate and collaborate with the ChessBlitz YorkU executive team to facilitate communication of club events and announcements through the social media outlets utilized by ChessBlitz YorkU;
* Have a good understanding of UI/UX;
* Take quality event photos, post-processing them, and publish them on CBYU’s social channels; and
* Be comfortable with design software including Canva, Adobe Suite, MS Paint.

Article 8.9 CCL Manager
* This position is limited to one (1) individual
The CCL Manager must:
* Be familiar with CCL regulations;
* Be present at every CCL game to support CBYU’s players in the CCL;
* Be able to effectively solve any issues that shall arise, including but not limited to, cheating, no-shows, rescheduling and internet issues.

Article 9.1 Election Process
1. The election process applies to the following positions:
   a. President
   b. Financial Coordinator
   c. Event Manager
   d. Social Media Coordinator
   e. Outreach Coordinator
   f. Tournament Organizer & Director
   g. CCL Manager
2. Executive Elections:
   a. must be held at least once a year.
   b. have at least one week notice given prior;
   c. have the nomination period between April 25 and May 5 of every year;
   d. have the campaign and voting period between May 6 and May 20 of every year;
   e. have the ChessBlitz YorkU Chief Returning Officer supervising the electoral process. The ChessBlitz YorkU Chief Returning Officer  must be unbiased and approved by the Executive Committee. The ChessBlitz YorkU Chief Returning Officer must count all votes;
   f. have only registered ChessBlitz YorkU members vote;
   g. have the voting take place by secret ballot;
   h. are open to all interested candidates that are ChessBlitz YorkU members;
   i. have the nomination period include all those interested in executive roles getting nomination signatures from eligible voters;
   j. have a candidate considered elected to the Executive Committee if they receive a majority vote by the voters;
   k. have a candidate considered acclaimed to the Executive Committee if they run unopposed;
   l. have, in the case of a tie, another Executive Election where the only candidates are the tied ones;
   m. have all ChessBlitz YorkU members notified by the ChessBlitz YorkU Chief Returning Officer of the election results at most 48 hours after the campaign and voting period;
   n. have the leaving executives transfer all knowledge and credentials that is vital to ChessBlitz YorkU operations to the new ChessBlitz YorkU Presidents at most 48 hours after the ChessBlitz YorkU Chief Returning Officer releases the election results; and
   o. have, in the case of a by-election or vacancy of an executive, the above regulations followed.
3. An interested candidate is running for President or Finance Coordinator, they cannot run for any other position.
4. If an interested candidate wants to run for more than one executive role in an Executive Election, they must indicate which one of those roles they would hold during the term of the Executive Committee if they were elected to more than one role. The role that they indicate will be known as the candidate's preferred executive role. They are allowed a maximum of three executive roles they can run for.
5. If a candidate is elected to more than one executive role in an Executive Election, then the role they will hold during the term of the Executive Committee is the candidate's preferred executive role that they indicated in the Executive Election. The candidate is removed from the other roles that they were elected to and, when possible, those roles must be given to the next highest-voted candidate for those roles.
6. If there were no candidates for an executive role in an Executive Election, then the role can be appointed through the application process.
7. If there were no candidates for the President or Finance Coordinator positions another election shall be run.
